{"name":"Island Palm","hex":"#6c7e71","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"island","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, totally surrounded by water.","A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, partially surrounded by water; a peninsula; a half-island."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To surround with water; make into an island.","To set, dot (as if) with islands."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/island"},{"term":"palm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various evergreen trees from the family Palmae or Arecaceae, which are mainly found in the tropics.","A branch or leaf of the palm, anciently borne or worn as a symbol of victory or rejoicing."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The inner and somewhat concave part of the human hand or other primate hand that extends from the wrist to the bases of the fingers.","The corresponding part of the forefoot of a nonprimate mammal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/palm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Island","blocks":[{"text":"An island or isle is a piece of land, distinct from a continent, completely surrounded by water. There are continental islands, which were formed by being split from a continent by plate tectonics, and oceanic islands, which have never been part of a continent. Oceanic islands can be formed from volcanic activity, grow into atolls from coral reefs, and form from sediment along shorelines, creating barrier islands. River islands can also form from sediment and debris in rivers. Artificial islands are those made by humans, including small rocky outcroppings built out of lagoons and large-scale land reclamation projects used for development."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg/330px-Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Island","w