ptive radiation of finch A (Geospiza magnirostris) into three other species of finches on the Galapagos Islands. Due to the absence of other birds, Darwin's finches adapted to new niches. Their seed-eating beaks evolved to handle foods such as nuts, fruits, and insects.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFinchadaptiveradiation.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Dronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg/500px-Dronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Dronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg/1280px-Dronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Dronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg/500px-Dronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The extinct Dodo is an example of island gigantism.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Breadfruit_%28Artocarpus_altilis%29%2C_Malaysia.JPG/500px-Breadfruit_%28Artocarpus_altilis%29%2C_Malaysia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Breadfruit_%28Artocarpus_altilis%29%2C_Malaysia.JPG/1280px-Breadfruit_%28Artocarpus_altilis%29%2C_Malaysia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Breadfruit_%28Artocarpus_altilis%29%2C_Malaysia.JPG/500px-Breadfruit_%28Artocarpus_altilis%29%2C_Malaysia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A breadfruit tree in Malaysia, used in Polynesia for making an edible breadfruit paste.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABr